            ]
          },
          "text": "I have a genuine question for @elonmusk and @nikitabier. 😤👇\n\nRT this if you’re tired of being ignored as a Premium user on X.\n\nIs X a social platform or a never ending experiment called X(Beta)?\n\nMonths ago, I was posting hundreds of replies a day to grow engagement.\nThen I read your rules.\nI stopped forced interaction.\nI started acting like a “natural user.”\nI focused on original, educational content.\n\nI followed the rules. The result?\n\nEven with 13,000+ Premium followers, my posts barely reach 100–200 views not even my own audience.\n\nSupport says: “Wait, it will fix itself.”\nIt’s been one month. Nothing changed.\n\nIn February 2026, you announced over $1 billion in annual revenue from Premium subscriptions.\nBut let’s be honest this is not success.\n\nWhen algorithms constantly change, people don’t grow they restart.\nNew accounts. New subscriptions. Same disappointment.\n\nIf this is real success, then why don’t you also publish\nhow many users cancelled their Premium subscriptions?\nBe transparent.\n\nRevenue earned from confusion and instability is not innovation!\nit’s profit built on user frustration.\n\nWhile low effort repost accounts get boosted endlessly,\nrule following creators quietly disappear.\n\nSo I’ll ask again:\nIs X a platform for creators or a private island(!) where user frustration is the entertainment?"
        },
